<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-eugracilis-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Schnakenberg Turing wavelength at 1.5 µm in Drosophila eugracilis (Pass 1 focal run) — MorphoEval overall 76.7/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 1 integrates Schnakenberg kinetics at gamma=1 on a 128^2 periodic grid (12 focal wavelengths, 17.820 µm window) and fixes the length unit so the analytic lambda_c is 1.485 µm. The saturated field is an ocellar spot lattice (activator std 1.26, 93 foci). Analytic lambda 1.485 µm versus FFT lambda 1.809 µm. Raw Otsu arm fraction on the gallery plate is 0.141 and KS luminance distance to the render is 0.343. No gamma sweep, no equal-diffusion control, and no series Pearson/RMSE are stored in pass1_metrics.json. Overall 76.7/100 (faithfulness 73.0, reproducibility 85.2); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 0c76d15d; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 86, Morphological realism / specimen match 72, Parameter expressivity 60, Morphometric validation 66, Source and data traceability 90, Code-to-model traceability 84, Reproducibility package 82. Output judged: docs/media/drosophila_eugracilis_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-eugracilis-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 0c76d15d, image/png, 476053 B, 1792×1148 px, artifact_sha256 6d16c18dee30d5d187f765e4dcb77304ca63822df7e92fc4c0a1e3ea7710ffbc (sha256 6d16c18dee30d5d187f765e4dcb77304ca63822df7e92fc4c0a1e3ea7710ffbc), spec_fingerprint 4cd159ca0e54b6b9882667ea66ee1c36e85c25ecfd3d9cd25e35efca3e35cc7f. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 4cd159ca0e54b6b9882667ea66ee1c36e85c25ecfd3d9cd25e35efca3e35cc7f; artifact_sha256: 6d16c18dee30d5d187f765e4dcb77304ca63822df7e92fc4c0a1e3ea7710ffbc; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/drosophila_eugracilis_turing_wavelength_s0/drosophila_eugracilis_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=aeae6e2ee094bbd3..., datasets/drosophila_eugracilis_turing_wavelength_s0/drosophila_eugracilis_turing_wavelength_s0_specimen.jpg=f3705e558598c7f5..., datasets/drosophila_eugracilis_turing_wavelength_s0/paper_citations.bib=963fd37391fe7bc7...}. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing 1952 dispersion relation and a critical wavenumber. | Schnakenberg 1979 two-species kinetics. | Tanaka, Barmina and Kopp 2009: sex-comb rows rotate in some Drosophila lineages and are born longitudinal in others. | Ready, Hanson and Benzer 1976: the retina is a periodic neurocrystalline lattice.; reconstructed_in_script: Length unit chosen so gamma=1 yields the assigned 1.485e-6 m detail wavelength. | gamma=0.5 for D. erecta and 1.180 µm for D. ficusphila as the chronoseries contrast at this scale.; transfer_boundary: The gallery JPEG is a project spiral plate with a 100 µm bar, not an SEM of a D. eugracilis ocellus.; does_not_claim: That 1.485 µm was published as a measured eugracilis rhabdomere or sex-comb spacing. | That D. erecta is a stratigraphic ancestor. Position 13/41 is the flattened Holocene chronoseries. | The sibling 101 µm primordium parameters or DOI 10.1016/j.ydbio.2009.04.012, which Crossref assigns to a different paper.." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: {'id': 'R1', 'item': 'Run a gamma sweep spanning D. erecta (0.50), D. eugracilis (1), and D. ficusphila, and record analytic versus FFT wavelength.'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R2', 'item': 'Add the equal-diffusion negative control D_u = D_v and report final activator std against the Turing run.'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R3', 'item': 'Replace the grain-dominated raw Otsu perimeter with a blurred arm segmentation and keep value distinct from the reference.'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R4', 'item': 'Report series goodness-of-fit: Pearson r, RMSE, and the plate-versus-render KS statistic, with value not equal to reference.'}" ;
    pk:hasScore 7.67e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

